{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/357745-tell-me-about-your-cults","id":357745,"title":"Tell me about your Cults!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-02T14:41:37-08:00","id":357745,"title":"Tell me about your Cults!","content":"I'd love to hear about what clever organizations you folks have built for your lovely Arisen.<br /> <br /> Nakht\u00e9 the Bloody Tempest (Su-Menent/Decree of Ab) was a barbarian chieftain who converted to worship of the Judges after his tribe was conquered, and in the millenia since he's continuously found willing servants in the ranks of humanity's armies. In his last awakening (North Africa, WW2), Nakht\u00e9 was courted by the Third Reich's archaeologist-occultists, but was impressed by the bravery of the British forces and sided with them to devastating effect. A young Captain Churchill of the Special Air Service came to be his most trusted ally during that awakening, and once Nakht\u00e9 returned to deathless sleep, Churchill set out to build a private military company with a global reach.<br /> <br /> Two generations later, Churchill's grandson is the head of Solar Barge Security, an international corporation that recruits from a number of Western armed forces. Solar Barge is perfectly a perfectly legitimate corporate entity with holdings across the world and a reputation for taking the dirtiest of jobs. They bring in millions of dollars per year, and only a select few on the board of directors know anything of the eccentric &quot;Mr. Nakht\u00e9,&quot; officially listed as a majority shareholder and ARCHINT consultant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T18:09:49-08:00","id":373947,"title":"","content":"Though I don't have Mummy, my research into the subject has given me an idea I think might be neat to use in a game. <br /> THE CHURCH OF THE ANGEL DESCENDING<br /> It's a nice little town; quiet, low crime, maybe an hour away from the Greater Orlando Metropolitan Area[replace with Chronicle's city if necessary]. In this town, A lot of people belong to the town's church. It's a nice, quiet, tolerably low amounts of fire and brimstone church, not really noticeable at all. Mostly so, I mean, they just have one little bit of teeny-tiny heresy... They have an angel in the Church's basement(the fact that it HAS a basement can probably be chalked up to the miraculous knowledge of Irem!). Their ancestors found him long ago in Europe. He was the one who taught them the special patterns to build their villages(to prevent miscarriages and encourage luck) and fields(to ensure the fertility and quality of their ancestor's grains and their own orange crop). In exchange, they have promised to aid him in his divine mission. He has been tasked to seek out strange relics, created by madmen who chose to seek the forbidden. But men were not meant to wield such power, and those who possess them suffer horribly. Their angel may claim these dark tools and leave his body to return to Heaven and disperse the Relic's power. He is not the only angel; never the less, many of these angels are fey, rebellious creatures, who demand worship from the mortals they meet, and are thus mot to be trusted. While they will not kill, they are more than willing to (apologetically) hold people against their will until they &quot;see reason&quot;, and more than one townsfolk who have moved to the big city still hold to their &quot;sacred duty&quot;.<br /> <br /> As one might guess, the &quot;Angel&quot; is actually one of the Arisen, a Lion-Hearted Tef-Aabhi named Ababius. What one might not guess(and what would horrify his fellow Arisen to know) is, while he is deceiving his cult about his nature, he is NOT deceiving them about his nature; he truly has become a Christian. He still serves the judges, both because one of the first things he remembers is the dangers Relics pose to mortals, but also because he is still loyal to his homeland and the Judges, his kings; he merely no long views them as his gods. Unfortunately, as he is aware, his justification is not exactly acceptable to his peers..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T22:12:25-08:00","id":374055,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough, MtC actually deals with how the Arisen view Christianity; the myth of Azar is similar enough to the story of Christ for many of them to simply assume the latter is the former, distorted through the lens of history. You could easily pull a Santeria on folks and pitch the Judges as minor saints, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}